model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Identity Center sessions remain encrypted server-side and separate from retained outside service OAuth accounts. Each tool call resolves one assigned account and role before requesting temporary credentials and signing its exact MCP request. Approval binds the target, arguments and saved connection revision; denial never obtains role credentials or dispatches a write. Interactive forms and opted-in reconnect use shared account acquisition, retain the saved account ID and choices, and preserve the previous session on cancellation. Protocol 37 retains protocol 36 account endpoint ownership and protocol 35 attribution, and the served framework pin and generated MCP assets match the prepared source. Canonical framework exports own their type declarations; method groups link to them so authoring reference data stays inside the upload budget."
    }
  }
}
